Asbestos Register Upgrade  Requirements Specification. 
Prepared for	Workstream 1A – Connecting Data
Prepared by	Victor Peters, Business Analyst
Version	1.0 – draft 
Date	16 November 2026


 1. Execute Summary
Today’s asbestos register in the contractor portal is a raw list of every survey live ever recorded in PIMS. Users need a true asbestos register: one clear, consolidated line per room or element for each property. 
This document sets out what users need, functional and non-functional requirements, risks, constraints and a list of what is to be delivered. The upgrade will be built on cleansed data in Microsoft Fabric. PIMS stays, and an updated Asbestos Register will be built on this Data
2. Scope 
This document captures the business needs for upgrading the asbestos register. It is the basis for agreeing priorities, design and a prototype, and it is not a solution specification.
In scope	Out of scope
Cleansing and consolidating asbestos data in Fabric into a property-level register	Handheld devices used by operatives
How register data is structured, sorted, filtered and searched	Standardising contractor survey or certificate formats, which are legal documents
Linking register lines to their source surveys and documents	Operative training on reading surveys
Automating survey and removal updates where safe to do so	
Improve asbestos information for customer letters	
Colour-coding features to show Asbestos detectability	
