4. Current state (as-is)
Asbestos information moves from survey contractors into PIMS and reaches users as one long, unconsolidated list.
•	A survey is requested (refurbishment, targeted or management). Its status is tracked on a Smartsheet fed by the contractor.
•	The contractor (currently Franks Portlock for all new surveys) emails the completed survey to the asbestos inbox.
•	Survey data is validated by hand, then loaded into PIMS in a weekly bulk upload, so there can be up to a week's delay.
•	Some teams skip the wait by saving surveys from the email into a house file for operatives.
•	Users see every line from every survey in the PIMS contractor portal. Positives are highlighted in red, the newest survey shows first, and there are basic filters.
•	When a removal is completed, the waste consignment note goes to Emma Jorgenson's team, who delete each matching line in PIMS by hand.
•	Customer letters embed a table pulled straight from PIMS.
