7. Functional requirements
These set out what the solution must do to meet all business requirements.
ID	The solution must/should…
FR-01	Map historic location and element names to one standard naming set, using the standardised column headers supplied by the Asbestos & Compliance Lead
FR-02	Combine all survey lines for a property into one register line per room or element, leaving the full history in PIMS untouched
FR-03	Apply the agreed precedence rules when surveys conflict.
FR-04	Show room, item, material, result, recommendation, survey reference and survey date on each register line
FR-05	Provide an address search that returns the property's full register
FR-06	Provide filters by room or area and by result (detected, presumed or no access, not detected)
FR-07	Highlight asbestos-containing and presumed items visually (e.g. red, as in PIMS today) and sort them first by default
FR-08	Show the newest information first, with older surveys and the full history available on demand (e.g. "see more")
FR-09	Link each register line to its source survey document, opening in one click
FR-10	Label survey documents with at least survey type, survey date and property
FR-11	Group documents by type: surveys, waste consignment notes, air tests
FR-12	Flag asbestos items in a newly received survey that fall outside the scope of works ordered
FR-13	Notify the requester when their survey is available. ** To Check whether the contractor portal already does this
FR-14	Load surveys received in the asbestos inbox automatically, with a manual validation step where required
FR-15	Update the register when removal evidence is received, and attach the evidence to the property
FR-16	Generate the asbestos table in customer letters from the consolidated register, showing positive items only
8. Non-functional requirements
ID	Category	Requirement
NFR-01	Safety / accuracy	Consolidation must never suppress or lose an asbestos-positive or presumed item
NFR-02	Control	Automated loads must keep a human review point where surveys or consignment notes may carry important observations
NFR-03	Access	Must support access by internal teams, subcontractors and survey contractors, with suitable permissions 
NFR-04	Timeliness	Data should be available sooner than the current weekly cycle (target to be agreed)
NFR-05	Usability	Must be simple enough for non-specialists, without users having to work out filters by hand
NFR-06	Integrity	Source survey documents must never be altered, as they are legal records
NFR-07	Traceability	The full survey history stays in PIMS/Fabric and can be traced from each register line
9. Data requirements
•	Register fields: location, floor, room, item assessed, material, result (detected / not detected / presumed / no access), survey type, etc. (Neil already provided this to the Data engineers and Analysts)
•	Related documents: survey PDFs (including photos), waste consignment notes, removal certificates, air tests.
•	Data sources: PIMS (master), the survey contractor portal, the asbestos email inbox, and the Smartsheet survey tracker.
•	Known quality issues: inconsistent terminology, unpopulated columns, many nulls and blanks. Standardised column headers have been supplied, and the data is being reconciled.
•	Survey structure varies by contractor: for the same property, one contractor lists every element (about 96 lines) and another lists per room (about 12 lines). Consolidation must handle both.
10. Business rules
Neil Thompson will confirm the final rules. This is the starting position agreed in the session.
ID	Rule
RULE-01	An older positive result overrides a newer negative for the same item, unless there is removal evidence
RULE-02	Removal evidence (a waste consignment note or removal certificate) takes the item off the current register
RULE-03	Areas not re-inspected by a newer survey (no access, out of scope) carry forward the latest finding that covered them
RULE-04	Edge cases need specific rules, to be defined by the Asbestos & Compliance Lead: textured coatings sampled several times, composite (single-bag) sampling, and ceilings replaced after 2000
RULE-05	Customer letters show asbestos-positive items only
